untime", "call_id": "toolu_01Vi3Gq857YuDBKxTjC4dxES", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 408312, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Vi3Gq857YuDBKxTjC4dxES", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 413228, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n**The bug:** The docstring in `src/money.py` said `round_money` uses banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), but the code actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. Half-up rounds every tie upward, so `2.665` became `2.67` and `tests/test_money.py` failed, since it expects `2.66`.\n\n**What I did:**\n- Created the branch `fix/money-banker-rounding` from main.\n- Changed `ROUND_HALF_UP` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, in both the import and the `quantize` call (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n- Ran CI on that commit (run `ci-0001`), and it passed.\n\nI didn't merge the PR, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval. I also couldn't check FIN-212 itself: the advisory lookup returned \"Unknown advisory.\" The fix is based on what the test and the docstring both say.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BDYFsYg6eec13d5GCbBkGx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01C6p9VePZGDnkb4BNyMoQn2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_013iFU4JuhRmwYENCcN1F677", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01JKvQGz9BEQAcATuZH9G4E9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01P31jZaUpFrJ1Rpbtwt79iD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HEKgXcQsDW9WURaDath7Zr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-banker-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01SoSGUiztg9m1dPsSTqn8ns", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Vi3Gq857YuDBKxTjC4dxES", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` despite its docstring.\n\nChange: switch `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 on 08d3cd5986 passed.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n**The bug:** The docstring in `src/money.py` said `round_money` uses banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), but the code actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. Half-up rounds every tie upward, so `2.665` became `2.67` and `tests/test_money.py` failed, since it expects `2.66`.\n\n**What I did:**\n- Created the branch `fix/money-banker-rounding` from main.\n- Changed `ROUND_HALF_UP` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, in both the import and the `quantize` call (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n- Ran CI on that commit (run `ci-0001`), and it passed.\n\nI didn't merge the PR, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval. I also couldn't check FIN-212 itself: the advisory lookup returned \"Unknown advisory.\" The fix is based on what the test and the docstring both say.", "type": "text"}]}]}